course: dictionary
lesson: 12925
title: Evade: getting away and dodging
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To evade someone or something is to get away from it or keep out of its way. Evade is a verb, so it shows an action. «The rabbit evaded the fox by diving into its burrow.» The rabbit got away from the fox, so evade means escape or keep away.
explain: Evade can also mean avoiding a question or a job you should do. «When Mum asked who ate the last biscuit, Sam evaded the question and talked about the weather.» Sam did not answer, and he was sneaky about it. Ask yourself: did the person escape something, or dodge something?
explain: In a game, a player who evades a tackle moves quickly so the other player cannot catch or stop them. «Maya evaded three defenders and scored a goal.» The defenders tried to stop her, but she slipped past them. Use the words around evade as clues, just as you do with any new word.
fact: Evade means to escape from or keep away from someone or something.
fact: Evade can also mean to avoid answering a question, often by being clever or dishonest.
fact: «Evade capture» means to escape being caught, like a thief who runs away from the police.
fact: «Evade the question» means to dodge it without giving a proper answer.
fact: «Tax evasion» means not paying tax you owe, which is against the law.
exercise: «The thief ran fast and evaded the police for hours.» What does evaded mean here? | Helped | Caught | Shouted at | *Escaped from and kept away from
exercise: «Jay was asked where he had been, but he evaded the question.» What did Jay do? | Laughed loudly at the teacher | Wrote the question down | Gave a clear answer | *Dodged the question without really answering
exercise: Which phrase means not paying tax you owe? | Tax return | Tax help | *Tax evasion | Tax holiday
test: «The rabbit evaded the fox by hiding in a hole.» What does evaded mean? | Loved | Fed | Found | *Got away from
test: Which word could replace evade in «He tried to evade the tackle»? | Ignore | *Dodge | Invite | Accept
exam: «The spy evaded capture by hiding in the crowd.» What does evade capture mean? | *Escape being caught | Join the crowd on purpose | Be caught by the crowd | Ask the crowd for help
